Getsome wrote:
> I was thinking about this today and to me it seems impossible to ascend
> with no wishes / genocides or bones files.
> Has anyone been able to do this regularly?

Yes, quite easily possible. And add polypiling to these "conducts".
Regular ascenders can avoid any of these helpful conducts if they
like.

Wishing; guaranteed only at castle. At that time you really don't need
wishes any more. But it helps overcome boring procedures due to your
player lacking some helpful item.

Genocides; possible only using some very rare scroll that you won't
get very often in the early game. Even if your mind got sucked beyond
recognition by some mindflayer it doesn't prevent you from ascending,
your game just takes longer because of all the re-identification and
re-exploration you have to do. Liches may be a pain, and you may have
to kill a lot of monsters the tedious way. Other monsters are rarely
worth a genocide in the mid to late game.

Polypile; just a means of shortening the game to obtain some items
that you haven't seen yet and want to get.

Bones; somewhat special, no conduct. There were times when I died
regularily after encountering a bones level with, e.g., nice artifact
weapons, primarily due to the character becoming burdened and bad
object/stash management on my side. So I'd say my life expectation got
better with ignoring the bones levels ;-)  But, again, it's just a
situation to get some equipment that you don't have (or don't have a
comfortable amount of) in an easy way. You even reduce your chances if
the bones file is loaded with crappy artifacts that reduce your chance
to get something better.

